{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06PV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Y} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-flat-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dcd052d177e27930a6a0dd0c49c287570b732b7849d07937611fe07fd1f6c6ab", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fbe03f844f6cdee237acce01caacbd09905ef599248d83f0e10facca6ba9a976", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be morphisms of\nalgebraic stacks. If <MATH_0002> is flat\nand <MATH_0003> is surjective and flat, then\n<MATH_0004> is flat.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3bc3b1358c97b476ef58d882e501279adf1dc009f90cc66d37be8180e3df464b", "unit_id": "tag:06Q0:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06PV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$W$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0003": "$V$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\to W \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to V$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\to W$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0010": "$U \\to V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-flat-permanence}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f2ebf27fd961fcde16bc2a549f97bcfc4767b68e1759b31b7084fc06bc5a79af", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:56571bc170a4e4567a2fcf19cc2585236cca971f677ec017e60606698c21a1a2", "source_text": "Choose an algebraic space <MATH_0001> and a surjective smooth morphism\n<MATH_0002>. Choose an algebraic space <MATH_0003> and a surjective smooth\nmorphism <MATH_0004>. Choose an algebraic space\n<MATH_0005> and a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0006>.\nWe know that <MATH_0007> is flat and that <MATH_0008> is flat.\nAlso, as <MATH_0009> is surjective we see that\n<MATH_0010> is surjective (as a composition of surjective morphisms).\nHence the lemma reduces to the case of morphisms of algebraic spaces.\nThe case of morphisms of algebraic spaces is\nMorphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3d55ba607ad72cbc5837e83d4d4e8e68459daba79a0b6c10780f5810df882c93", "unit_id": "tag:06Q0:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06PV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Spec(A) \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0005": "$|\\mathcal{Y}|$", "MATH_0006": "$|\\mathcal{X|} \\to |\\mathcal{Y}|$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(A') \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & \\mathcal{X} \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\Spec(A) \\ar[r] & \\mathcal{Y}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$A \\to A'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-definition-extension-valuation-rings}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-lift-valuation-ring-through-flat-morphism}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5017c0945619f5f0d0a3052e9899749aa253234d39a5d8d041436186b455fee7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ee804376b91374ff514dcc2ad2bf3f38b04185e54d78a59336a2d9b628458f2f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a flat morphism\nof algebraic stacks. Let <MATH_0002> be a morphism\nwhere <MATH_0003> is a valuation ring. If the closed point of <MATH_0004> maps to a\npoint of <MATH_0005> in the image of <MATH_0006>,\nthen there exists a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0007>\nwhere <MATH_0008> is an extension of valuation rings\n(More on Algebra, Definition\n<REF_0001>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8d27a84e77bed0ae1f2d36569804b6e84ca0013c0407c91859d99d6199004464", "unit_id": "tag:0DN5:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06PV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}_A \\to \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0003": "$|\\mathcal{X}_A| \\to |\\Spec(A)|$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Y} = \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to \\Spec(A)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-flat}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-points-cartesian}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-lift-valuation-ring-through-flat-morphism}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:27af57f3ee1f875c0ef1103861dd5266e7d7ed0b05c282248244412355b9c4a2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a543f5915191b1d09605f956b8f00fd2abbe595dddb420082e6e966f0faf5213", "source_text": "The base change <MATH_0001> is flat\n(Lemma <REF_0001>) and the closed point of\n<MATH_0002> is in the image of <MATH_0003>\n(Properties of Stacks, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nThus we may assume <MATH_0004>. Let <MATH_0005>\nbe a surjective smooth morphism where <MATH_0006> is a scheme.\nThen we can apply Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma\n<REF_0003>\nto the morphism <MATH_0007> to conclude.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:02d6097fe7561708147fabc34717fbb9289cde54f93a99362277470859c11d34", "unit_id": "tag:0DN5:proof"}
